# SketchUp Ruby Script Plugin Rules

## API Compliance#
- Follow the **Official Sketchup Ruby Api 2026** exclusively.
- The Ruby API is brittle — never invent or assume classes, methods, or constants. If unsure, consult the documentation before writing code.
- Reference: https://ruby.sketchup.com/

## Code Style
- Match the existing coding style in any file you edit.
- Keep all Ruby Script files **Under 600 Lines**. If a file exceeds this, split it into logically cohesive modules.

## Plugins Folder
`C:/Users/Administrator/AppData/Roaming/SketchUp/SketchUp 2026/SketchUp/Plugins`

---

## BEFORE Writing Any Code — Mandatory Steps

1. **Build A Full File Tree** of the **Particular Plugin We Are Editing** Folder, including all subfolders at every depth level.
2. **Trace Module Relationships** — the project is heavily modular; logic is spread across multiple files and levels.
3. **Never Create A New File** without first confirming the function does not already exist elsewhere.
4. **Map Existing Functions** relevant to the task before writing anything new.

> Skipping these steps risks duplicating logic that already exists in another module.

---

## AFTER Writing Code — Mandatory Checks

- Verify no functions have been duplicated across the codebase before delivery.
- Confirm all API classes and methods used are valid in SketchUp Ruby API 2026.